course: dictionary
lesson: 15581
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and swipe is a good example. «Swipe left to see the next photo» means move your finger across a screen. «The bear swiped at the fish» means hit with a big swinging movement. The words around swipe tell you which meaning is right.
explain: Look at the clues. «Tap your swipe card on the reader to open the gate» is about a card passed over a reader, not a finger on a screen. Ask yourself: what is happening here? Then try the meaning that fits and check that the sentence makes sense.
explain: Swipe can also be informal, which means everyday talk rather than formal writing. «Someone swiped my pen at lunch» means someone stole it quickly. Swipe can also be a noun: «The article was one big swipe at the coach» means an unkind comment that criticises someone.
fact: «Swipe» means to move your finger across a screen to change what is shown.
fact: «Swipe» means to pass a card through or over a reader, to pay or open a door.
fact: «Swipe» means to hit, or try to hit, with a big swinging movement.
fact: «Swipe» can mean to steal something quickly, which is informal speech.
fact: A «swipe» is an unkind comment that criticises someone.
exercise: «Swipe left to see the next photo.» What does swipe mean here? | Pass a card through a reader | *Move your finger across a screen | Steal quickly | Hit with a big swinging movement
exercise: «The bear swiped at the fish and missed.» What does swiped mean? | Paid for lunch with a card | Moved a finger across a screen | *Hit, or tried to hit, with a big swinging movement | Stole the fish quickly
exercise: «The article was one big swipe at the coach.» What is a swipe here? | *An unkind comment that criticises someone | A quick nap | A way to open a door | A small piece of paper
test: «Tap your swipe card on the reader to open the gate.» What does swipe mean? | Hit with a big swinging movement | *Pass the card over a reader to open the gate | Steal quickly | Move your finger across a screen
test: «Someone swiped my lunch box while I was in the queue.» What does swiped mean? | Paid for it with a card | Hit with a big swinging movement | Moved a finger across a screen | *Stole it quickly
exam: Jayden says, «Swipe always means moving your finger on a phone.» Is he right? | No, it means to sing loudly | Yes, that is the only meaning | Yes, but only on tablets | *No, swipe can also mean pay with a card, hit, steal, or make an unkind comment
